  "name": "Pokémon Battle Tour 09",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "Pokémon Battle Tour 09 (ポケモンバトルツアー09) was the big Pokémon event of summer 2009, held at shops across Japan, mostly AEON group stores, on one day each between 11 July and 6 September 2009, in place of the Battle Road tournaments of earlier summers. It offered card battles, a beginners' class, a lottery and a chance to try the new Pokémon HeartGold and SoulSilver games, and everyone who took part got Mewtwo 049/DPt-P, drawn by Ken Sugimori.\n\nIts Knockout Battle had a standard league with 60-card decks and a half league with 30-card decks. Three straight wins in either brought a silver Victory Medal showing Arceus, 036/DPt-P, and in the standard league the gold one too, 051/DPt-P. Heatran 050/DPt-P was the one new card in the tour's Challenge Deck, a 30-card Fire half deck sold only at its venues.",
